---
description: Multplx operating and contributor context for Cursor CLI
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` for the operating contract; `CLAUDE.md` points to that same contract.
Use your current task assignment to determine whether you coordinate or execute work.
For development of Multplx itself, read `VISION.md` for checkout restrictions and contributor context.
Keep Cursor sandboxing enabled and use the assigned isolated checkout.
Nested delegation is available through Cursor's native tools and Multplx sessions.
The `subagentStart` hook records provider evidence when Cursor emits it and otherwise leaves the recovery limit explicit.
When developing Multplx itself, do not run Multplx operational session start in this development checkout.
